[2017-11-15T16:55:36Z | jebrando | comment]
The change to remove the abandoned enum from the MQTT sample has been checked in.

body:
Memory leak about calling mallocAndStrcpy_s

OS and version used: Non-RTOS, bare metal system
SDK version: IOTHUB_SDK_VERSION "1.1.20"

At "mqtt_client.c" #450:
```
    if (result == 0 && mqttOptions->willMessage != NULL)
    {
        if (mallocAndStrcpy_s(&mqtt_client->mqttOptions.willMessage, mqttOptions->willMessage) != 0)
        {
            LOG(AZ_LOG_ERROR, LOG_LINE, "mallocAndStrcpy_s willMessage");
            result = __FAILURE__;
        }
```
We want to copy the ```mqttOptions->willMessage``` to ```mqtt_client->mqttOptions.willMessage``` by calling ```mallocAndStrcpy_s```, but neither the caller and the callee functions free the existing memory of ```mqtt_client->mqttOptions.willMessage```, if it is not null, before assigning a new memory block for it, this will cause a memory leak.

Same behaviors at #434, #442, #458 and #466.

