completeLogin - is a moment when server sends back OK to hardware for Login command. But as you can see hardware sent 2 commands before login finished.

if doing something like:

LCD.print(0, 0, "Hello");
LCD.print(0, 1, "World");

only "World" will be displayed on the bottom line if the app was closed while sending this data, but opened after some time has passed since sending both commands ... Both should be displayed.

```java
public boolean hasWidgetsByDeviceId(int deviceId) {
        for (Widget widget : widgets) {
            if (widget instanceof OnePinWidget) {
                OnePinWidget onePinWidget = (OnePinWidget) widget;
                if (onePinWidget.deviceId == deviceId) {
                    return true;
                }
            }
            if (widget instanceof MultiPinWidget) {
                MultiPinWidget multiPinWidget = (MultiPinWidget) widget;
                if (multiPinWidget.deviceId == deviceId) {
                    return true;
                }
            }
            // ADDITIONAL CHECK
            if (widget instanceof DeviceSelector) {
                DeviceSelector deviceSelector = (DeviceSelector) widget;
                if (ArrayUtil.contains(deviceSelector.deviceIds, deviceId)) {
                    return true;
                }
            }

        }
        return false;
    }
```

