I just pushed an update to `tuya-cli` that allows you to perform a MITM attack on your phone and easily acquire device parameters.  Update with `npm i @tuyapi/cli -g`, then you should be able to run `tuya-cli list-app`.  I also updated the [documentation on setup](https://github.com/codetheweb/tuyapi/blob/master/docs/SETUP.md).

Unfortunately, I realized after all this while writing the documentation that Android doesn't support installing root certificates for arbitrary apps.  So Android users will have to use the old setup method for now (sorry about that).  If you have any ideas on getting Android to work as well, I'd love to hear them.

