body:
Fifo component takes the last element out of the queue making it partially a LIFO.

```java
...
if (!run) {
    break;
}
next = queue.remove(queue.size() - 1);
consumer.signal();
...
```
Until it's full it will behave erratically, when it fills up, it works properly, if it doesn't discard the inbound envelopes. When it starts to empty, it emits the oldest few elements.

Kura 3.1.0, develop branch

