[2016-07-14T12:33:37Z | cdealti | comment]
@pstanton Thanks for reviewing the documentation and the implementation. Please see my notes below.

> "job.id" is missing.

Agreed. We will add it to the documentation.

> "dp.download.protocol" should not say "default HTTP" this suggests it is not mandatory. Maybe "e.g. 'HTTP'" would be better, or make it default/non-mandatory in the implementation.

I believe it's indeed mandatory:

```
    setDownloadProtocol((String) request.getMetric(METRIC_DP_DOWNLOAD_PROTOCOL));
        if (getDownloadProtocol() == null) {
            throw new KuraInvalidMessageException("Missing download protocol!");
```

so the documentation should say "either HTTP or HTTPS".

> "dp.install.system.update" should state "mandatory", or default to "false" in the implementation.

I believe it's indeed mandatory:

```
setSystemUpdate((Boolean) request.getMetric(METRIC_DP_INSTALL_SYSTEM_UPDATE));
        if (getSystemUpdate() == null){
            throw new KuraInvalidMessageException("Missing System Update!");
```

> in addition, the dpName and dpVersion should definitely be split and sent in different metrics to match the input parameters, as considered in the comment in the below snippet:

I agree. The problem is that this would break compatibility with the Cloud Platform which might expect the concatenated name. It would be better to add two new metrics `dp.name.2` and `dp.version.2` to reflect the value of `dp.name` and `dp.version` in the request.

Incidentally, I believe the implementation needs to be... well... polished ;)

