body:
With the latest OH2 (from this afternoon, so I think it probably includes the latest ESH changes) I get exceptions when requesting GET rest/things -:

``` json
{
  "error": {
    "http-code": 500,
    "exception": {
      "class": "java.lang.NullPointerException"
    }
  }
}
```

While this reporting might be great for a UI in that we can report something more useful than just error code 500 (although in reality, not much more useful) there's no way that I've found to work out the root of the problem?  Are these errors reported somewhere or are they swallowed up and all we get is this error on the REST interface - it's just not very useful for debugging.

I have a feeling there's something wrong with thing labels since I'm trying to implement the new label support in HABmin and I may have saved a null label or something.

