In fact, that is quite normal. The algorithm works back from years to seconds, pruning whatever it does not need anyways. The problem lies in the last 5-6 lines of the trace log. It should propose. 2017-01-04 16:20:00.000 as final candidate.

[2017-01-11T18:19:28Z | kgoderis | comment]
@kaikreuzer I just created and tested https://github.com/eclipse/smarthome/pull/2798 in a simple use case scenario (see below). Can you test it with the persistence service?

FYI, by putting the maximum number of candidates to 2 (instead of 1), the case whereby the final candidate would be equal to the start time is covered, e.g. at least one candidate will be later than the start date, and thus retained after pruning. It potentially doubles the number of candidates after each round of expansion, but this has little or no impact on performance.

