When using the color temperature channel of LIFX bulbs, it slightly changes the tone, but it does not switch to "white mode". Instead, I expect it to always switch to a white tone (cold to warm), but not keep hue/saturation in place from before (same as in the LIFX app when switching from "color" to "white tone" color wheel).

This is afaik a regression - I remember that we discussed that in the past already and it had been fixed.

@wborn Could you please have a look?

So far, the Paper UI showed the textual percent value for sliders. This does not seem to be the case anymore:

<img width="382" alt="screen shot 2017-05-25 at 16 18 00" src="https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/3244965/26453947/d470e036-4165-11e7-8d89-65150f70e2b1.png">

@aounhaider1 & @htreu Any idea what might have caused this change?

Image displayed in the Basic UI (by adding an Image element in the Sitemap) are not resized properly). In my setup I'm trying to display a screenshot from a security camera that has a 1920*1080 resolution, and the  image is always bigger than its container.

Adding this to the page's css (via the Chrome dev console) fix the issue:

img {
    max-width: 100%;
    max-height: 100%;
}

I don't have much experience in Web development, so it might not be the right fix :).

This is working fine in the Classic UI

I really want to keep all my config for things together (in the .things file rather than the PaperUI option) but adding a Lifx light I want the powerOnBrightness to be the previous power off value and setting it to empty in the PaperUI things config works fine when you add it (as a thing) using PaperUI  BUT if you want to add it in the .things file then following the demo.things file [here](http://docs.openhab.org/addons/bindings/lifx/readme.html#demothings) causes the default value of '100' to be used... e.g.

    Thing lifx:colorlight:living [ deviceId="D073D5A1A1A1" ] {
        Channels:
            Type color : color [ powerOnBrightness= ]
    }

IF however you use a value between 0-100 it DOES use that. e.g.

    Thing lifx:colorlight:living [ deviceId="D073D5A1A1A1" ] {
        Channels:
            Type color : color [ powerOnBrightness=75 ]
    }

No idea why we haven't seen this before, but just ran into this one:

```
Circular reference detected trying to get service {org.eclipse.smarthome.config.core.ConfigDescriptionRegistry}={service.id=127, service.bundleid=86, service.scope=bundle, component.name=ConfigDescriptionRegistry, component.id=119}
