The initial analysis above is not the full problem. Even when no fields/methods from AbstractSystemOfUnits leak the compiler is not happy with static imports:
When using 
```
import o.e.s.core.library.unit.SmartHomeUnits;

// and later

Unity<?> ampere = SmartHomeUnits.AMPERE;
```
in the code directly the class compiles fine w/o errors.

When doing

```
import static o.e.s.core.library.unit.SmartHomeUnits.AMPERE;

// and later

Unity<?> ampere = AMPERE;
```

the compiler complains about `The type tec.uom.se.AbstractSystemOfUnits cannot be resolved. It is indirectly referenced from required .class files` (SmartHomeUnits directly extends `AbstractSystemOfUnits`).

However, when using
```
import static o.e.s.core.library.unit.SIUnits.CELSIUS;

// and later

Unity<?> celsius = CELSIUS;
```

the class compiles fine (with SIUnits extending SmartHomeUnits).
I don't understand this behaviour yet.

The workaround as of now is to not statically import SmartHomeUnits units.

[2018-04-16T14:21:11Z | htreu | comment]
I posted [this stackoverflow](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/49859548/java-import-static-fails-when-imported-class-extends-3rd-party-lib) to gain some insight. Feel free to comment here or there.

[2018-04-24T14:19:10Z | htreu | comment]
