body:
I am sending a POST request to `/rest/rules` with the following content:

```
{
  "templateUID": "SampleRuleTemplate",
  "configuration": {
    "condition_operator": ">",
    "condition_constraint": "6"
  }
}
```

I expected a rule to be created based on the referenced template, but if I request the created rule, I get

```
  {
    "enabled": true,
    "status": {
      "status": "IDLE",
      "statusDetail": "NONE"
    },
    "triggers": [],
    "conditions": [],
    "actions": [],
    "configuration": {
      "condition_operator": ">",
      "condition_constraint": "6"
    },
    "configDescriptions": [],
    "templateUID": "SampleRuleTemplate",
    "uid": "rule_6"
  }
```

So the reference to the template is not correctly replaced by the rule that is defined by it.

I started using an ItemStateEvent Condition, but it is never satisfied.
After some debugging I have a look at the "isSatisfied" method of the EventConditionHandler.

The code looks like:

``` java
        Event event = inputs.get("event") != null ? (Event) inputs.get("event") : null;
        if (event != null) {
            return isConfiguredAndMatches(TOPIC, event.getTopic()) && isConfiguredAndMatches(SOURCE, event.getSource())
                    && isConfiguredAndMatches(PAYLOAD, event.getPayload())
                    && isConfiguredAndMatches(EVENTTYPE, event.getType());
        }
        return false;
```

If I looked at the content of <code>inputs</code> my event is not named "event", but "trigger_1.event". If I changed the strings, the condition is working.
I assume the naming "event" is correct and the function that fills the map have to change the "trigger_X.event" naming to "event".

But I do not know any of the automation code...
Which code has to be fixed?

