[2018-07-15T10:20:14Z | maggu2810 | review:COMMENTED]
You should use `System.currentTimeMillis()` instead of `ZonedDateTime.now()`.
We are not interested in the date / time at all but only the time that has been elapsed.
For the delta we don't want to depend on the system time of the machine itself, so if the system time is changed by the user or some services (e.g. NTP) this should have no relationship to the delta.
What we want to use is a monotonic time and for so `System.currentTimeMillis()` is our candidate.

