hey thanks for the answers.

@kleini you are right, I should not have skipped steps. Anyways since I started using homie some time ago I have been having issues connecting to the MQTT broker (mosquitto), the only thing that solved it was that nasty delay call on the main loop. Oddly enough the delay makes it extremely stable, like in days without disconnecting. I will create a separate ticket for that with a bare bones sketch to illustrate what's going on and maybe you can help out. PS: I am an atheist so I don't beg to god ;)

@amayii0, about the delay you are right, about the Wire.beginTransmission that would not be possible since you need to do that every time you send a command over the I2C bus marking the beging and the end of the payload beign sent.

