I haven't however not understood it was renamed. Interesting to know! Debugging using serial output is a PITA.

My usual issues related to actually running the code were related to improper definition of boards. Usually about the size of the flash.

I don't know Sloeber at all, for my case I'd lookup:
- http://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/platforms/espressif8266.html
- https://github.com/amayii0/Homie-Photocell/blob/master/platformio.ini#L13 : a Sample of mine, working on a D1 Mini clone (see https://www.instructables.com/id/Building-Homie-Devices-for-IoT-or-Home-Automation/#step4)

[2017-06-01T14:04:13Z | jantje | comment]
@ThomasH-W 
I tried it here. The hardware debug fails to compile because homie uses FS.h which does not exists in  1.6.5.947-g39819f0.
It compiles fine against the thread "MovingToV2_3" however I never succeeded in getting debugging working in V2_3.
So for now I think hardware debugging is not an option

[2017-12-12T19:34:36Z | jantje | comment]
Debugging should be an option now with release V4.2 which supports debugging with esp 2.3

[2019-04-04T11:59:10Z | stritti | comment]
I close this issue. Seems to be solved otherwise reopen it.

