----UPDATED
**The reason was in the Arduino IDE 1.8.1-1.8.2 versions.**

Are there any restrictions to the firmware name length? If I set firmware name longer than 14 symbols I get truncated output while nodeMCU starts. 

**Example 1.** _Everything is OK:_

```
#include <Homie.h>

void setup() {
  Serial.begin(74880);
  Homie_setFirmware("uuuuurrrgggnnn", "1.0.0");
  Homie.setup();
}

void loop() {
  Homie.loop();
}
```
Result:
![homienobug](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/6689478/26483222/28340e2c-4216-11e7-93e8-86f67b372485.gif)

**Example 2.** _Getting output truncated. The longer firmware name is - the more output truncated._
```
#include <Homie.h>

void setup() {
  Serial.begin(74880);
  Homie_setFirmware("uuuuurrrgggnnnRRRRRR", "1.0.0");
  Homie.setup();
}

void loop() {
  Homie.loop();
}
```
Result:
![homiebug](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/6689478/26483190/f2697b10-4215-11e7-972e-fd3128d9db8d.gif)

