I am trying to run a gateway that takes its metadata from Watson IoT. Whenever the metadata changes in Watson IoT the propertyChangeListener should fire.
When doing this for a ManagedDevice, this works fine, however for  ManagedGateway I either get an NPE or the Metadata in Watson IoT is wiped out or overwritten when the gateway starts.

The sample code below may be used to try out the concept:
- Define a Gateway in your Watson IoT instance
- Update the 4 constants to match your settings
- Run this code as a Java application
- Update the metadata in Watson IoT for the Gateway
- And watch the propertyChangedListener fire
- Restart this Gateway and watch what happens to the metadata you just entered. It is gone.

For ManagedDevices it is possible to use option 3. But for ManagedGateways this does not work.

I think this is a bug at the following line:

https://github.com/ibm-watson-iot/iot-java/blob/f2a732a87dad7f17ee0fd654f5b95e9a11ef669c/src/main/java/com/ibm/iotf/devicemgmt/gateway/ManagedGateway.java#L667

The jsonMetaData.isJsonNull() is always false because jsonMetaData is a JsonObject which cannnot equal a JsonNull.


```
