@CindyXing @sids-b i think we need to cache these changing events on cloudhub side.
in cloudhub, we store change events in `channelPool` 
```
// ChannelEventQueue is the channel implementation of EventQueue
type ChannelEventQueue struct {
	ctx         *context.Context
	channelPool sync.Map
}
```

but `channelPool` is map, it`s value is no-buffer-channel,   we need to change this channel to a queue to catch this changeing event.

 and this queue need support upstate event function 。 if we receive a new event which has the same attributes(Group, Source,UserGroup, ID, ParenetID) as an event int he queue. we only update the event in the queue.  If the new event is different from all the event properties in the queue, we need push it to the queue.

