[2017-07-23T16:17:58Z | kruemelro | comment]
Hi, 
thanks, i haven't had the serial-debug on my mind. I switched it on and, as you mentioned, the Node don't receive the Message. 
I know the smartsleep function from mySensors waits 500ms befor go to sleep, but the SLEEP message from NodeManager cames instant afer the sensor loop. I inserted a wait code into the sleep function at NodeManager.cpp and know it works as it should.

Here a snippet from what i've changed:

```
//wrapper of smart sleep
void NodeManager::_sleep() {
  // reset the last interrupt pin
  _last_interrupt_pin = -1;
  // wait for incomming config Messages
  #if REMOTE_CONFIGURATION == 1
      #if DEBUG == 1
          Serial.println(F("WAIT FOR CONFIG"));
      #endif
      wait(500);
  #endif 
  // calculate the seconds to sleep
  long sleep_sec = _sleep_time;
```

