Hi,

This doesn't work, the sensor gets ignored
``` 
  ChildId=nodeManager.registerSensor( SENSOR_HCSR04);
  SensorHCSR04 *Dist=(SensorHCSR04 *)nodeManager.getSensor(ChildId);  
  Dist->setTriggerPin(6);
  Dist->setEchoPin(5);
```

This is because _pin (in the parent object) isn't being set even though the trigger and echo pins are being set in later calls. This causes the sensor to be ignored in the loop.

The work  around is to set the pin like;

```
   ChildId=nodeManager.registerSensor( SENSOR_HCSR04, 6);
```
but it would be nice if the setTriggerPin method also set  _pin in the parent.

