## Bug Report

### Expected Behavior

`System.sleep(D2, RISING, 1)` should halt the MCU and turn off the Network radio, and wait for 1 second before or until a rising edge is observed on D2.  In this case `D2` is shorted to `GND` so there should not be a chance of it seeing a rising edge and it should sleep for 1 second.

### Observed Behavior

Tested on Device OS `1.1.0-rc.2`, `1.2.0-beta 1.` and `1.2.1-rc.1`.  `System.sleep(D2, RISING, 1)` randomly returns immediately without indicating any type of error.  Note periods below that are not LOW for 1 second.

Can reproduce in MANUAL, SEMI_AUTOMATIC and AUTOMATIC system modes.

<img width="1232" alt="Screen Shot 2019-05-23 at 5 14 09 PM" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/2249224/58295234-b7deb080-7d93-11e9-8ab4-0b7aed3248b3.png">

### Steps to Reproduce

Run the test app on a Gen 3 device (Argon, Boron and Xenon tested) and observe an inconsistent 1/2Hz waveform on A5.  A5 used to as the output to avoid any pin adjacent to D2 in case of capacitive coupling.

### Test App

```c
SYSTEM_MODE(MANUAL);
SYSTEM_THREAD(ENABLED);

void setup() {
  delay(10000); // for development purposes so we can get into dfu mode after
                // reset
  pinMode(A5, OUTPUT); // debug
  pinMode(D2, INPUT);
  digitalWrite(D3, LOW);
}

void loop() {
  System.sleep(D2, RISING, 1); // D2 is tied to GND

  if (System.sleepError() > 0) {
    RGB.control(true);
    RGB.color(255, 0, 0);
    while (1) {
    }
  }

  digitalWrite(A5, HIGH);
  delay(1000);
  digitalWrite(A5, LOW);
  // System.sleep() should complete the other 1 second low time
}
```

### References

Thanks for the report and testing [Kevin!](https://github.com/iitgrad)

## Bug Report

### Expected Behavior

System.sleep(X) sleeps the network radio (or Mesh radio for Xenon) for X seconds.

### Observed Behavior

It doesn't stay asleep, sometimes for the prescribed time, sometimes 1 second, other times a very short amount.

### Steps to Reproduce

Run the included test app on Argon on 1.2.1-rc.1, and see similar results to below:

