## Bug Report

### Expected Behavior

When there is a valid IP connection, DNS lookup on LTE based u-blox SARA-R410M-02B modules should return a valid response.  This can be done via `Cellular.resolve(host)` API or when used internally for resolving the Particle Cloud IP address.

### Observed Behavior

The DNS client fails to return results and continuously times out after a variable period of time via 8.8.8.8:53 over UDP on SARA-R410M-02B.  This can be immediately, 1 hour or potentially 24 hours or more later.  This appears to be a bug in the u-blox modem, potentially with older revisions of firmware.

**Workaround:** Currently, the known recovery mechanism is to detect the DNS lookup failure and power cycle the modem with Cellular.off() / Cellular.on() or call a System.sleep() command that results in the modem powering off temporarily.

### Steps to Reproduce

This can be reproduced with the following test app.

Eventually this test app will start to publish `0.0.0.0` as the resolved IP address, due to DNS lookup timing out with no response from Google DNS.

### Test App

```c
#include "Particle.h"
SerialLogHandler logHandler(LOG_LEVEL_ALL);
system_tick_t lastDNSLookup = 0;
void setup() {
}
void loop()
{
    if (millis() - lastDNSLookup >= 120000UL) {
        Serial.println("\r\n\r\nDNS lookup =====================================");
        IPAddress ip = Cellular.resolve("google.com");
        Particle.publish("Google HOST IP", String(ip), PRIVATE, NO_ACK);
        lastDNSLookup = millis();
    }
}
```

✏️ Particle is currently investigating this issue with the intention to implement a fix in the next Device OS release 1.4.1 default, scheduled for October 14th, 2019.

