System.sleep(5) not turning Wi-Fi back on after 5 seconds.  System.sleep is supposed to turn of Wi-Fi and continue running code, which it does.  However after 5 seconds Wi-Fi is not turned back on and reconnected automatically, which is not stated anywhere but implied with `sleep(5)`.
https://community.particle.io/t/not-sure-how-to-use-sleep-mode/13082/4

I have created an app to demonstrate this, if you read the comments you'll see that the D7 LED is toggling every second, which makes it easy to count to 20, after which the RGB should be WHITE.  5 seconds later it should be blinking green but does not.  then at the 30 second mark we force a reconnect.  At the 40 second mark the system will try to sleep(5) again, and this process will repeat over and over.
