### Description:

We have seen occasionally that during an attempt to set up new wifi credentials the app will hang indefinitely as it attempts to connect to the Photon wifi. Quitting the app and retrying does not fix the problem, and we are forced to reset the photon in order to successfully send wifi credentials. This has been hard to reproduce consistently, so while the the following steps are more specific (resending duplicate credentials), it produces the same behavior very consistently. No timeouts or Setup Failure screens are encountered even after waiting 5+ minutes for the connection to resolve (possibly a secondary issue).
### Steps to Reproduce:
1. Flash Photon with the test user program code below
2. Set Photon into Listening Mode by holding right button 
3. Using wifi setup app, send correct router credentials to Photon
4. **Important** once Photon LED goes to breathing cyan, _immediately_ force-quit setup app (double-tap home and swipe up)
5. Without resetting Photon, repeat steps 2-4 a few times
6. If a failure/hung app occurs, close app and attempt to retry the normal setup process
7. typically, I see it takes one or two times before the behavior is seen - setup app hangs indefinitely at the screen below, and subsequent attempts to setup have the same behavior, requiring a reset to fix.

![image](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/12628878/10773271/c49dcdf0-7cd0-11e5-9144-47c517886cf0.png)

Note that these steps are just the reliable way to reproduce, but I have also seen this during normal operation - ie. changing credentials and waiting for the app to fully complete the checklist. It just appears that when I exit the app early it is much more reliable, and I would think that shouldn’t cause the Photon to get into the state where you need to reset.
### Test Code to Reproduce:

``` cpp
#include "application.h"

SYSTEM_MODE(MANUAL);
SYSTEM_THREAD(ENABLED);

STARTUP(WiFi.selectAntenna(ANT_AUTO));

void setup()
{
  Serial.begin(9600);

  WiFi.on();
  WiFi.connect();
  Particle.connect();

  Serial.println("Example program");

  Particle.variable("wifiSSID", WiFi.SSID());
}

void loop()
{
  Particle.process(); 
}
```

